Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Simple Chemical Reaction Networks", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.506895078210659*^9, 3.506895081203388*^9}, {
  3.755918593929102*^9, 
  3.755918599895072*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e665a5fd-4ec6-4b9a-a1fb-\
c780f9182647"],

Cell["\<\
We explore a few networks, just to illustrate how easy it is to play.

The rxn[ ] statement indicates the reactants, products, and rate constant.  \
Note that when a rxn[ ] statement is displayed, it gets printed such that it \
looks more like you would expect.

Note that when a reaction has no products, that is indicated by placing a \
constant where products would be listed -- in this case 0, but any other \
constant would give the same result.  Similarly, for zero-order reactions \
that consume no reactants, a constant is placed in the reactant slot.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.693186213042845*^9, 3.693186221185954*^9}, {
  3.69318630670045*^9, 3.693186327610448*^9}, {3.693186392702433*^9, 
  3.693186456169381*^9}, {3.693186668465563*^9, 3.6931866720684223`*^9}, {
  3.693246071236302*^9, 3.693246072876423*^9}, {3.693246143033906*^9, 
  3.693246180138476*^9}, {3.693246331425003*^9, 3.6932463400241632`*^9}, {
  3.693246374785656*^9, 3.693246425191392*^9}, {3.755918614061541*^9, 
  3.755918651329892*^9}},
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.9, 0.8],ExpressionUUID->"7af86dde-d1dd-45d1-88c7-3f21780a0feb"],

